Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||03-27-2001||07:35 AM||||Call a different dealer with your VIN #.<BR>Sounds like the one you contacted is to lazy to check!<BR>There may be a way on-line to check, but I have no idea what it would be.<BR>Check out this link, it's a place to start.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/recalls.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/recalls.html</A> <P>(copy and paste if needed)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||03-27-2001||02:38 PM||||my pontiac dealer gave me new exhaust manifolds and e-brake cables. parts and labor free. I have 86 SE too||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||03-27-2001||08:43 PM||||Dealers and GM are growing more dificult to deal with in most cases. Do a search to see what other people have gone thru.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.gov" TARGET=_blank>www.nhtsa.gov</A>  you can find the sumaries of the recall(s) in question.<P>The recall procedure specified that a label be placed on the car with the recall information. The small white label contains the dealer ID, date, and Recall ID. These labels are to be posted conspicuoously in the engine bay.<P>If you can't verify a recall was done....<P>check more than one dealler. Do this in person. document who you talk to.<P>call GM. Tell GM that dealers can't/won't help and that you will call NHTSA unless these issues are resolved. Again document who you speek to at GM.<P>If they refuse to help call NHTSA and begin a formal complaint. GM is required by federal law to fix recall items or prove they have already been done.<P>search the forums. the full text of the L4 fire recall letter to owners is here someplace. I posted it. It includes the info where to call NHTSA. You can probably find it on the NHTSA web site. (A sumary of the L4 fire recall is in my cave.)<P>NOTE! This applies only to vehicle safety recalls NOT TSB's. The Fire prevention recalls come under this. I beleive there is a brake recall for manual transmission V6.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.alldata.com" TARGET=_blank>www.alldata.com</A>  also has sumaries of the recalls. If you subscribe you can get the full text and all the TSB's as well.||||reg||1
